WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.860
It's Friday, November 6, and this is the Singularity Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.930
Here are the last 24 hours in superintelligence, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.590
They heard you. Two days after the vote,

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:21.080
OpenAI promised to pay its data centres' power bills.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:25.880
And Meta's president admits building new ones is going to be harder.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:39.120
OpenAI's new GPT-6 Cyber hunts security holes, and OpenAI rates it critical.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.420
It found 81 serious new bugs in Firefox.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.770
For now, only vetted security teams get it.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.660
Meanwhile,

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:52.030
OpenAI says ChatGPT now handles about a fifth as many searches as Google.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.300
And Greg Brockman says it should be ready to go public in 2027.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.220
Now, the money. AI stocks led a slide that took the S&P 500 down more than 3%.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.300
A year ago, a rival predicted Agility would go bust.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.650
Instead, the humanoid maker just went public.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.140
Valued at $2.5 billion, on $1.8 million in sales last year.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.300
Meanwhile, about 600,000 Nvidia chips are reportedly stuck in Hong Kong,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.300
waiting for China's approval.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.500
In Japan, Taisei's giant tunnel-boring machine ran itself with AI,

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.290
and beat veteran operators on precision.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.490
And a young start-up is offering $200,000 f

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.540
or each of five unsolved materials problems.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.170
The catch? AI agents sent shopping got it wrong nearly half the time.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:54.110
And one congresswoman wants superintelligence banned outright,

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:55.460
and advanced AI paused.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.060
Now, the machines.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.450
Unitree's founder says his robots paint and play chess, untrained.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:15.470
But China blocked SoftBank's $5.4 billion takeover of ABB's robotics business.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.570
And in Australia, living human brain cells steered a robot dog to its target.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.900
Turns out when people speak up, the builders listen. So keep talking.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.240
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.780
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.370
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.200
You've been watching the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
